\ Ms. Pac-Man on telic's bitmaps, keyboard and synthesizer.
\
\   ./telic examples/ms-pac-man.telic
\   ./telic examples/ms-pac-man.telic --level 6
\
\ Keys: the arrows steer, p pauses, return starts, escape quits. A direction
\ pressed before a turn is taken at the turn, cutting the corner. On a
\ gamepad the d-pad or the left stick steers and start begins a game and
\ pauses it.
\
\ The arcade's four mazes, each in its own colors, change with the acts:
\ levels 1-2, 3-5, then four levels each, the last two mazes alternating.
\ The fruit enters through a tunnel, hops along its fixed route to the ghost
\ house, laps it, and leaves by another tunnel; eat it on the way for 100 to
\ 5000 points. Blinky chases, Pinky ambushes four tiles ahead, Inky aims
\ past Blinky, Sue chases from afar and retreats up close; while scattering,
\ Blinky and Pinky head for a corner chosen at random. An energizer turns
\ them blue for a time that shortens with the level, and eaten ghosts score
\ 200, 400, 800, 1600. Three lives, an extra one at 10,000.
\
\ The rules, the sources the mazes and routes were transcribed from, and the
\ sound are described in examples/mspacman/game.telic. The sprites, the
\ maze drawing and the music are this program's own.

"mspacman/game.telic" load

play
